{"units": [{"id": "gar-note1", "translation": "The use of this particle, which is never placed at the beginning of a sentence or verse, but is introduced after one or more words, is to give the reason for and demonstrate the truth of what has been said in the preceding sentence in one or more words, whether by the same or another person. Since there is an infinite abundance of examples of this kind in every genre of writing, I am content, after a few examples from one play, to indicate the rest, as Wellauer did, by verse numbers alone. Pr. 7, 17, 27, 29, 34, 51, 59, 86, 107, 128, 133, 148, [182], 184, 224, 244, 310, 338, 341, 342, 345, 361, 394, 401, 441, 524, 542, 617, 645, 649, 685, 701, 716, 718, 740, 750, 766, 780, 785, 803, 829, 862, 897, 905, 918, 940, 963, 968, 995, 1008, 1012, 1016, 1032, 1037, 1039, 1056, 1064, 1068, 1076. Sept. 4, 17, 22, 42, 52, 59, 64, 77, [113], 120, 141, 189, 224, 244, 281, 295, 321, 379, 403, 411, 427, 458, 500, 509, 511, 539, 592, 601, 644, 662, 680, 684, 741, 766, 772, 1009, 1037, 1069, 1074. Pers. 1291, 97, 102, 126, 172, 175, 211, 234, 247, 255, 291, 341, 355, 373, 392, 431, 444, 459, 466, 491, 504, 548, 590, 592, 603, 631, 649, 652, 707, 713, 765, 767, 772, 784, 792, 802, 816, 821, 834, 838, 851, 913, 924, 942, 949, 1002, 1009, 1033. Ag. 10, 14, 32, 76, 105, 134, 154, 214, 217, 222, 253, 259, 267, 326, 343, 350, 354, 381, 422, 433, 461, 469, 500, 506, 522, 524, 532, 534, 555, 559, [560], 584, 601, 650, 654, 674, [761], 800, 832, 834, 838, 871, 880, 904, 916, 948, 953, 966, 1001, 1003, 1040, 1056, 1075, 1082, 1095, 1106, 1110, 1112, 1133, 1137, [1147], 1186, 1187, 1226, 1280, 1284, 1354, 1365, 1369, 1374, 1437, 1478, 1486, 1523, 1564, 1583, 1605, 1630. Ch. 3, 16, 32, 47, 75, 101, 103, 132, 175, 187, 207, 234, 250, 278, 286, 299, 305, 360, 374, 375, 388, 402, 421, 453, 483, 504, 505, 520, 523, 543, 560, 637, 641, 665, 668, 679, 686, 702, 726, 748, 753, 754, 755, 773, 859, 874, 891, 905, 989, 990, 1021, 1023, 1033, 1054. Eum. 33, 38